WEBVTT

00:00:19.462 --> 00:00:21.504
(GREETING IN FRENCH)

00:00:21.839 --> 00:00:24.966
I'm sorry,
I don't know what you just said at all.

00:00:25.301 --> 00:00:27.552
Welcome to the French Ministry of Magic.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.346
What is your business, please?

00:00:30.514 --> 00:00:34.517
(SLOWLY) I need to
speak to Tina Goldstein.

00:00:34.602 --> 00:00:39.606
She's an American Auror
working on a case here.

00:00:44.487 --> 00:00:45.737
We have no Tina Goldstein here.

00:00:46.948 --> 00:00:49.658
No, I'm sorry.
There must be some sort of mistake.

00:00:49.742 --> 00:00:52.702
See, I know she's in Paris.
She sent me a postcard.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:54.454
I brought it.
I can show it to you. Here.

00:00:54.538 --> 00:00:57.207
Maybe you can help me find it here.
It's just in here. Oh!

00:00:58.376 --> 00:01:01.086
Rabbits! If you can
just wait one moment!

00:01:01.254 --> 00:01:03.630
I know it's in here somewhere.
I definitely packed it.

00:01:03.798 --> 00:01:05.048
Where is it?

00:01:05.216 --> 00:01:06.549
One second.

00:01:06.717 --> 00:01:08.385
What did I do with you?

00:01:10.388 --> 00:01:11.596
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

00:01:16.602 --> 00:01:18.103
(ELEVATOR DOORS CLOSING)

00:01:34.578 --> 00:01:35.912
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

00:01:43.337 --> 00:01:45.046
JACOB: Could we at least
stop for coffee or...

00:01:45.131 --> 00:01:46.131
NEWT: Not now, Jacob.

00:01:46.215 --> 00:01:48.717
JACOB: Chocolat chaud or...
Just for a second?

00:01:53.222 --> 00:01:54.556
- I don't know.
- NEWT: This way. Come on.

00:01:54.849 --> 00:01:58.184
JACOB: Pain au chocolat?
Half a croissant and a bonbon?

00:01:58.352 --> 00:01:59.519
NEWT: This way.

00:02:04.608 --> 00:02:05.692
Jacob!

00:02:17.038 --> 00:02:18.872
(ECHOING CHATTER)

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:20.790
Jacob?

00:02:20.958 --> 00:02:22.876
- (ECHOING CHATTER CONTINUES)
- (THUNDER RUMBLING)

00:02:47.109 --> 00:02:48.777
(ECHOING CHATTER CONTINUES)

00:03:03.918 --> 00:03:05.126
(CHATTER STOPS)

00:03:07.171 --> 00:03:08.380
(WOMAN SPEAKING FRENCH)

00:03:09.799 --> 00:03:11.299
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

00:03:26.607 --> 00:03:27.941
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:04:03.811 --> 00:04:05.103
She's home.

00:04:39.054 --> 00:04:40.472
(DOOR CREAKING)

00:04:41.557 --> 00:04:42.557
(BOTH SPEAKING FRENCH)

00:04:52.568 --> 00:04:53.902
CREDENCE: (IN ENGLISH) Are you Irma?

00:04:55.529 --> 00:04:57.530
Are you Irma Dugard?

00:04:59.074 --> 00:05:03.453
I'm sorry.
Your name is on my adoption paper.

00:05:05.331 --> 00:05:06.748
Does this make sense?

00:05:08.959 --> 00:05:11.211
You gave me
to Mrs. Barebone in New York.

00:05:30.689 --> 00:05:32.690
I am not your mother.

00:05:32.858 --> 00:05:34.317
I was only a servant.

00:05:38.489 --> 00:05:40.740
You were so beautiful a baby.

00:05:43.285 --> 00:05:45.370
And you are a beautiful man.

00:05:56.048 --> 00:05:58.383
I did not want to leave you there.

00:05:59.009 --> 00:06:00.843
CREDENCE: Why didn't they want me?

00:06:05.516 --> 00:06:08.393
Why is your name on my adoption paper?

00:06:08.561 --> 00:06:11.563
I took you to Mrs. Barebone

00:06:13.315 --> 00:06:15.608
because she was supposed
to look after you.

00:06:17.444 --> 00:06:18.861
(WIND WHOOSHING)

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:28.788
(NAGINI GASPS)

00:06:32.293 --> 00:06:33.418
(YELPS)

